1
00:00:05,077 --> 00:00:09,017
Whiskers and Luna's World. Episode six. Deserts!

2
00:00:16,833 --> 00:00:21,490
Luna, find me the warmest, sunniest place on your globe. For a nap.

3
00:00:21,690 --> 00:00:24,969
Hmm. How about a desert? Like the Sahara, here in Africa!

4
00:00:25,169 --> 00:00:27,693
What makes a desert a desert? Is it the heat?

5
00:00:27,893 --> 00:00:31,967
Nope! A desert is a place where very little rain falls. Hardly ever!

6
00:00:38,513 --> 00:00:40,948
No rain? No baths? Perfect!

7
00:00:41,148 --> 00:00:42,534
Hold on to the cushion!

8
00:00:53,523 --> 00:00:55,742
Up into space they flew!

9
00:01:01,654 --> 00:01:04,996
See the yellow patches? Those are deserts, all over the world.

10
00:01:09,638 --> 00:01:13,418
This giant one is the Sahara. The biggest hot desert in the world!

11
00:01:13,618 --> 00:01:15,951
Wow! It covers about a third of Africa!

12
00:01:19,324 --> 00:01:21,785
So it's the world's biggest litter box.

13
00:01:21,985 --> 00:01:22,828
Whiskers!

14
00:01:38,895 --> 00:01:42,389
They landed in the Sahara. Phew, it was hot!

15
00:01:42,589 --> 00:01:44,528
Look! The sand is all in waves!

16
00:01:49,171 --> 00:01:53,139
Those are sand dunes. The wind blows the sand into hills.

17
00:01:57,782 --> 00:02:01,220
Hello! I'm Humphrey the camel. Welcome to my desert.

18
00:02:01,420 --> 00:02:03,374
Humphrey, does it ever rain here?

19
00:02:03,574 --> 00:02:06,537
Hardly ever. Some years, not a single drop!

20
00:02:06,737 --> 00:02:09,356
Oh, I know! Your hump is full of water!

21
00:02:16,537 --> 00:02:18,310
Hmm. Nothing's coming out.

22
00:02:18,510 --> 00:02:22,719
Hee hee, that tickles! My hump isn't full of water. It's full of fat!

23
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:34,050
The fat is my food store. And I can go many days without a drink.

24
00:02:34,250 --> 00:02:38,249
I knew that. I was testing your hump on purpose. It passed.

25
00:02:41,305 --> 00:02:43,515
Hop on! I know a green place.

26
00:02:55,138 --> 00:02:58,048
Over the dunes, they found an oasis.

27
00:02:58,248 --> 00:03:02,358
An oasis is a green spot in the desert, with water and palm trees!

28
00:03:06,366 --> 00:03:08,589
Psst! Down here! I'm Fizz, a fennec fox!

29
00:03:08,789 --> 00:03:10,490
Wow! Your ears are huge!

30
00:03:10,690 --> 00:03:14,372
My big ears let heat out, to keep me cool. And they hear everything!

31
00:03:19,650 --> 00:03:24,353
Mine too. I can hear a tin of tuna open from three rooms away.

32
00:03:27,409 --> 00:03:29,216
But at night, the desert gets cold!

33
00:03:29,416 --> 00:03:30,864
Cold? In the desert?

34
00:03:31,064 --> 00:03:34,205
Yes! There are no clouds, like a blanket, to keep the warm in.

35
00:03:45,829 --> 00:03:51,252
Brrr! Hot all day, and cold all night? Make up your mind, desert!

36
00:03:56,529 --> 00:03:58,233
But look at all the stars!

37
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:06,567
Here's a surprise. The biggest desert of all is icy Antarctica!

38
00:04:06,767 --> 00:04:08,789
But Antarctica is covered in ice!

39
00:04:08,989 --> 00:04:12,564
Yes. But hardly any snow falls there. So it's a desert too!

40
00:04:18,476 --> 00:04:22,010
Then my water bowl is a desert. Nobody filled it.

41
00:04:32,682 --> 00:04:37,402
Remember! One. A desert is a place where very little rain falls.

42
00:04:40,458 --> 00:04:44,497
Two. The Sahara, in Africa, is the biggest hot desert.

43
00:04:47,553 --> 00:04:50,902
Three. A camel's hump stores fat, not water.

44
00:04:58,083 --> 00:05:03,162
Quiz time! What makes a place a desert? Lots of heat, or very little rain?

45
00:05:06,535 --> 00:05:10,348
Very little rain! Even cold places can be deserts.

46
00:05:13,087 --> 00:05:16,928
Next. What is inside a camel's hump? Water, or fat?

47
00:05:20,301 --> 00:05:22,592
Fat! Not water, Whiskers!

48
00:05:30,408 --> 00:05:33,123
And with a twinkle, they were home again.

49
00:05:33,323 --> 00:05:36,632
Ahh. Home. No more sand. Well... a little sand.

50
00:05:36,832 --> 00:05:38,880
Goodnight, Humphrey! Goodnight, Fizz!

51
00:05:42,888 --> 00:05:46,549
Next time, the rainforests! Goodnight, sandy world.

